{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now","id":321617,"title":"How to intruduce new players to M:TAw right now?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-25T03:29:50-08:00","id":321617,"title":"How to intruduce new players to M:TAw right now?","content":"So I got asked by a friend of mine if I would be interested in Storytelling a Mage: The Awakening game for him and his friends. I ran a short-lived chronicle years ago, and he really liked the idea, but honestly it has been a while since I sat down with the books.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I am pretty sure that this would be the group's first exposure to the World of Darkness, new or old.<br /> <br /> As I recall, Awakening can get a little labyrinthine as you explore the spellcasting rules, so does anyone have any recommendations on teaching the game system and concepts to the players?<br /> <br /> System-wise, I know the paradox system is a little too soft. Should I house rule this to give Dox a little more bite? Any suggestions on house rules?<br /> <br /> What about ritual casting? Any recommendations on reeling in this aspect of the game?<br /> <br /> Also, While I have a decent collection of Awakening books, I don't have them all, and I know from reading the forum that certain paths and orders have evolved a bit from their core book presentation. I don't think it's quite fair to hand the players the various supplements and say &quot;If you really want to understand the Free Council, read this... the core book got some things wrong.&quot; So what is a ST to do?<br /> <br /> I know they are working on a 2nd edition of mage right now, and while I would love to wait for it to hit the presses, I know these things can take some time. Would you guys recommend trying the GMC rules for mage *before* the 2nd edition rule book is finished? Have you noticed any hiccups between how Mage rules work and how the GMC rules update works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","user":"Froggy711","date":". 11-25-2014, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T03:49:28-08:00","id":321644,"title":"","content":"Pretty much all of the issues you bring up are being addressed in the second edition, so it's kind of difficult to say anything other than &quot;wait for second edition&quot;. For example, a lot of the caveats and gotchas are being removed from spellcasting rules, paradox has been completely reworked from the ground up, ritual casting is totally redone, and the developers are working to clarify a lot of the misconceptions and misrepresentations in the original core book.<br /> <br /> The problem you mention with Paradox isn't necessarily that it's too lenient, but that it doesn't accomplish what it's supposed to - which is to create hubristic moral dilemmas. The key parts of 2nd edition Paradox are that it's always caused by your decisions, and can never hurt you. Paradoxes can only harm other people unless you specifically choose to contain it within yourself. The player is pressed with the dilemma of whether they choose to put themselves in danger by containing a paradox, or put innocent bystanders at risk by releasing the paradox and hoping the spell does what you wanted it to anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 11-25-2014, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T04:08:07-08:00","id":321649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now#post321617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I am pretty sure that this would be the group's first exposure to the World of Darkness, new or old.<br /> <br /> As I recall, Awakening can get a little labyrinthine as you explore the spellcasting rules, so does anyone have any recommendations on teaching the game system and concepts to the players?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can just start with <b>GMC</b> Sleeper characters for the story or two. Enough to get player basic rules, general mood of the world, and some gameplay before choosing the Paths. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T04:11:41-08:00","id":321650,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I will tell you, when I read the blog post on Paradox and Reach it really piqued my interest in 2nd edition Mage. I'll be honest, Awakening's paradox kind of felt like a weaker version of Ascension's... more predictable, lower risk, though easier to implement.<br /> <br /> I would rather wait until 2nd edition, but it hasn't even hit 2nd draft yet, so I have a wait ahead of me, and I think he was thinking sooner than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T04:19:51-08:00","id":321652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I recall, Awakening can get a little labyrinthine as you explore the spellcasting rules, so does anyone have any recommendations on teaching the game system and concepts to the players? </div> </div> </div>I recommend going over <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allegory_of_the_Cave\" target=\"_blank\">Plato's allegory of the cave</a>. It'll help the players get into the right mindset to understand how magic works conceptually. It helps explain things like why &quot;patterns&quot; work the way they do, and why the Prime arcana has &quot;phantasms&quot; (The phantasms are shadow puppets on the walls of Plato's cave). I wrote a short essay related to it <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/316071-interactions-between-symbols-patterns-and-the-fallen-world\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=321650#post321650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I will tell you, when I read the blog post on Paradox and Reach it really piqued my interest in 2nd edition Mage. I'll be honest, Awakening's paradox kind of felt like a weaker version of Ascension's... more predictable, lower risk, though easier to implement.<br /> <br /> I would rather wait until 2nd edition, but it hasn't even hit 2nd draft yet, so I have a wait ahead of me, and I think he was thinking sooner than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can try to go with the current rules and adapt them to GMC. There's a stop-gap set of GMC rules somewhere on these forums. Adapting the core WoD rules to GMC isn't that hard, and there's not much in Mage that has to be changed to fit GMC. At the same time, if you do go with 1st edition rules and ever decide to switch to 2nd edition, you're gonna have to relearn the new system which your players might not be happy about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, While I have a decent collection of Awakening books, I don't have them all, and I know from reading the forum that certain paths and orders have evolved a bit from their core book presentation. I don't think it's quite fair to hand the players the various supplements and say &quot;If you really want to understand the Free Council, read this... the core book got some things wrong.&quot; So what is a ST to do? </div> </div> </div>Really not much but learn the information for yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about ritual casting? Any recommendations on reeling in this aspect of the game? </div> </div> </div>Put a cap on the effects of ritual spells. Potency cannot go past your dots in the highest arcanum used in the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 11-25-2014, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T04:26:00-08:00","id":321656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=321650#post321650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather wait until 2nd edition, but it hasn't even hit 2nd draft yet, so I have a wait ahead of me, and I think he was thinking sooner than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Run a Mortal/Sleepwalker <b>GMC </b>game then for now. Put a <b>Mage</b> in the background, let players soak the Mysteries, give them supernatural Merits for now. If books would not come out for next few months - always you can use the Paths and Orders previews - groups would not change that match in final product from this that is shown in blog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-25-2014, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T04:29:21-08:00","id":321658,"title":"","content":"You'd also do well to give your group a brief summary of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gnosticism\" target=\"_blank\">Gnosticism</a>'s creation myth. It's basically the same as the Matrix and the Lego Movie, since they were heavily based on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T05:29:47-08:00","id":321721,"title":"","content":"As to mine previous idea of Sleepwalker <b>GMC</b> game:<br /> <br /> You can also make &quot;Sleepwalker&quot; PCs in to Proximi that are prepering for Awakening, when they discovered they heritage and Mysteries. It should be cool game to run for couple of months till proper 2ed will come out.<br /> <br /> So it would be like for PCs<br /> <br /> Sleepers -&gt; Sleepewalkers -&gt; Proximi<br /> <br /> Proximi can be even introduced on lower echelons of Orders. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And when 2ed comes out, you &quot;just&quot; makes some really big event, and they Awaken. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T05:31:14-08:00","id":321722,"title":"","content":"Or you could let them go in blind. Let them find out the meat of Awakening by virtue of play.<br /> <br /> For the waiting game, wyrdhamster's idea is quite a solid start. If your players are fine with it, let them start entrenched in the various cults and intrigues of the Awakened. Mages are supposed to be the ones that follow the truth, even though it hurts. If they could turn away from a mystery, they wouldn't have become mages in the first place.<br /> <br /> Let them earn their Awakening. <br /> <br /> Depending on your storytelling-pace, and your groups timetable, that could well last you until 2E is released (in general, everyone hopes for a 1. quartal of 2015 release)<br /> <br /> On your other questions.<br /> <br /> Personally, in the current 1E rules, I prefer a weaker Paradox for my players. They have little say when it happens or how. Frankly, its not fun when it happens at all.<br /> <br /> Rituals have never been a problematic issue in my campaigns. I encourge my players to go nuts. I'm prone to saying &quot;Yes&quot; more often than &quot;No&quot; if the question is &quot;Can I *?&quot; By the time the truly gamebreaking rituals ( eg healing 1 aggravated wound every nanosecond, deathstar laserpointers, combusting a sizeable portion of the visible universe) become feasible, your players understand just how many people would object to such spells being used and have the power and ressources to stop them.<br /> <br /> For the books, I understand just throwing books at your players is not quite what you want, but in regard to Awakening books, I fear its quite necessary. The setting lives on its supplements. If you think you know which order the would like, point them at the book. They might enjoy them more than you think.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI have long since forsaken mortal blood. It offers me nothing but the stale taste of mayflies. I have partaken of Luna's ever-changing children and dined on the scholars of Magic. I have bled monsters, born and created. No more. Tonight I drink the blood of gods and slake my thirst for another thousand years of night.\u201d","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/312-grunt","name":"Grunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T06:21:20-08:00","id":321754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=321656#post321656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Run a Mortal/Sleepwalker <b>GMC </b>game then for now. Put a <b>Mage</b> in the background, let players soak the Mysteries, give them supernatural Merits for now. If books would not come out for next few months - always you can use the Paths and Orders previews - groups would not change that match in final product from this that is shown in blog.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I completely agree with this. Some months ago I tried to play M:TAw after 8 years of no roleplaying, with a group of friends that had not played nWoD before, and it was also the first time I played Mage (and I was the ST), so it was kind of messy. The game stopped because of reasons, but I'm planning to start over again with the same group the next year, and I'm planning to do what Wyrdhamster is suggesting.<br /> <br /> Mage has a lot of rules and options and things to do, which is awesome, but it's a bit overwhelmig, specially to people who hasn\u00b4t played nWoD before. A Sleeper GMC game will help them understand the basic rules, how some entities behave (like ghosts and spirits) and you could set the mood with a paranormal investigation theme.<br /> <br /> I have a couple of questions about this too:<br /> <br /> In the path's spoilers they suggest some presonality traits for mages before their awakening (monotonous pre-Acanthus, identity crisis pre-Mastigos, possessive pre-Moros, OCD pre-Obrimos and autistic pre-Thyrsus)*, would you present the paths to the players when they are making their sleeper charachters, so they can add some of this traits?<br /> <br /> In the order's spoilers it says that the orders teach their ideologies to the Sleepers without revealing the supernal. I imagine that the GotV do it through the Labyrinth, the SL through the Cryptopoly and the FC through Sleeper groups, like political parties. How would the AA and Mysterium teach their ideologies?<br /> <br /> * This are an oversimplification of what was shown in the spoilers and I know that the archetypes (pre and post awakening) are suggestions for characters personalities and in no way mandatory, but I like the ideas that can sprout from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3456-sir-phobos","name":"Sir Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T07:22:41-08:00","id":321792,"title":"","content":"Strill: I hadn't ever thought of the prime illusions thing that way before. Cool idea. I am heading to bed now (I work nights) so I will have to read your essay later. Also the potency cap sounds like a simple solution.<br /> <br /> Wyrdhamster: You are probably right. I can probably even use the Mage NPC as a GM Mouthpiece to explain the gnostic/cave allegory concepts to them.<br /> <br /> Grunt: Hopefully I can guide them toward an awakening in such a way that they can earn it. But sometimes players just like to go with the flow, which isn't conducive to mystic revelation. =] I hope you are right about the release date. But without an official release date I am wary of basing my game timetable on it.<br /> <br /> Phobos: Thanks for the input. It sounds like from your experience starting as sleepers is the way to go. And I would like to hear peoples input on &quot;priming&quot; the sleeper characters for awakening as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T07:33:16-08:00","id":321800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=321754#post321754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage has a lot of rules and options and things to do, which is awesome, but it's a bit overwhelmig, specially to people who hasn\u00b4t played nWoD before. A Sleeper GMC game will help them understand the basic rules, how some entities behave (like ghosts and spirits) and you could set the mood with a paranormal investigation theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always all start my games that, because, most of the time, I don't have a group of mostly experienced players with <b>Mage</b>. Last chronicle we made a half-way with this and general <b>Mage</b> model when one, my dedicated and loyal player who played before in other game - become a Guardian testing other three &quot;Sleeper&quot; characters if they would fit Labyrinth ( and being Hieromagus, but it's completly irrelevant <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). When they started to Awaken, he become their first mentor ( but not most important one ).<br /> <br /> I run few games where PCs were (Sleepwalkers) Hunters unreaveling the big Mystery, that answer on which broke they Sleep, and they Awaken almost instantly at the end of &quot;season 1&quot;.<br /> <br /> I also run short game about Proximi, that really want to be proper witch, but still can't and she obsessively test her limits and Mysteries to get Awakening.<br /> <br /> All are great models to teach new players basic of game and make a big waiting for the 2ed bearable. Also, they will teach you <b>GMC</b> rules that are fundation of all 2ed games from World of Darkness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=321754#post321754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the path's spoilers they suggest some presonality traits for mages before their awakening (monotonous pre-Acanthus, identity crisis pre-Mastigos, possessive pre-Moros, OCD pre-Obrimos and autistic pre-Thyrsus)*, would you present the paths to the players when they are making their sleeper charachters, so they can add some of this traits?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I would now run a preAwakening game now, based on previews, I would go with other route her - first, as always, I would ask player about the Path they are aspire to. Proximi have them built in to them, but others you can always ask &quot;Choose two Arcana you want for PC, one will be more important for character&quot;. Probably they choose some Arcana that makes cool character &quot;refilling&quot; concept - like Mastigos with Spirit, becuase <b>player</b> wants to have Mind and Spirit, with first dominant. Then I would enforce in the story the life crisis on the PC the Paths are connected to - Acanthus would need to decide to forsake his all life background to search for Mystery the group is looking - or <b>she could not look for what she wants ever again. </b>Moros will need to &quot;let it go&quot; of his belongings, so he could fuel his reaserch. Obrimos will need to answer the questions on reality and his belief - in science or God - questioning. Connecting it with main plot of the game, with only a bit personal sidestep, would be best for this kind scenario. Those &quot;personality traits&quot; shown in previews are unimportant - life crisis in the play are. At the end of the game you will look on character and say &quot;Samael , when he was only John, was very possesive. But then he was Awakening as Moros he change after this and that ordeal&quot;. And a like - traits aren't really important in RPG, decisions are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=321754#post321754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the order's spoilers it says that the orders teach their ideologies to the Sleepers without revealing the supernal. I imagine that the GotV do it through the Labyrinth, the SL through the Cryptopoly and the FC through Sleeper groups, like political parties. How would the AA and Mysterium teach their ideologies?</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather envision Free Council introducing Sleepers by wierd punk concerts and obscures fanzines, totally off-blogers, than political parties, but that's me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For our London games I even made an &quot;Assembly of Awakened&quot;, general esoterics net forum that is heavily inflirtrated by Libertines users.<br /> <br /> Mysterium is all about Knowlegde, so secret &quot;facts&quot; is totally in their style - some unusual writings in the old book about verse in the folk song repeting the numbers - this kind of thing. Don't forget also they roots in Eleusinian Mysteries, so sects and cults also work for Mysterium dogma.<br /> <br /> I have a weakest understanding in the AA, but from they general backgrounds it could be groups like secetive police and militray task force, mafia famillies or even Zen monks making treaties about their belifes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-25-2014, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T08:02:13-08:00","id":321828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=321754#post321754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the path's spoilers they suggest some presonality traits for mages before their awakening (monotonous pre-Acanthus, identity crisis pre-Mastigos, possessive pre-Moros, OCD pre-Obrimos and autistic pre-Thyrsus)*, would you present the paths to the players when they are making their sleeper charachters, so they can add some of this traits?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would find it more interesting to just letting them play and when it comes time to Awaken and they have picked their Paths ask them (in or out-of-character) what makes Joe Z Obrimos. How did Jane A connect with the Lunargent Thorn? And so on. It helps break stereotypes and the players can come up with some really interesting ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T10:34:29-08:00","id":321948,"title":"","content":"Just a small note:<br /> 1 - If your players are new to nWOD, the Order politics may become confusing, so either create a strong backstory to explain why they SHOULD have each other's back and not their order's, or have all players recruited by the same order, and if variety is demanded by players, try to guide them into complimentary orders for your story.<br /> <br /> 2 - Try to keep all relationshhips dynamic and recoverable (at first), a 3 party relationship helps. (e.g. the player has a mentor (little 'm', not the Background, in the same Order and when the player wants to go against one party, the other can support their desire), It also help deflect punishment to the alternate party, when needed.<br /> <br /> 3 - If you browse through David's Broken Diamond campaign, he has the players in a New Cabal, since the Concilium politics, make growing any established cabal too threatening the D.C. Council.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:46:30-08:00","id":322371,"title":"","content":"As an addendum to Gideon's suggestions, make sure the PCs have a back-story establishing that they are used to working together. It's easy for mage games to become paralyzed by over-cautious introduction scenes (&quot;Does this guy know about magic?&quot;). Either place them all in a cabal together, or if you have them start as Sleepers, make sure they all know and work together pre-Awakening.<br /> <br /> In terms of the splats getting better fleshed out, here's what I've gathered:<br /> <br /> 1.Order Themes: Dave lists them here about mid-way through -&gt; <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/new-order/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/new-order/</a> I've found that first listing those gets players excited about the Orders in a way that reciting the Atlantean caste system does not. I think it's also more immersive, since &quot;Magic is Alive&quot; is a better guide for RPing a Mystagogue than &quot;scholar-mage, here's some doctrine bullet points.&quot; The &quot;scholar&quot; identity <i>is </i>central to the Order, but it's more meaningful when contextualized as &quot;Magic is Alive, therefore we should devote our lives to chasing it down and studying it with scholarly devotion.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. Path Themes: right at the beginning of this post -&gt; <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/pathfinding/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/pathfinding/</a> Unlike other WoD lines, Mages deliberately make themselves supernatural. There are no accidental Awakenings; someone finds their Lighthouse and signs their name by becoming Obsessed with a Mystery (or Mysteries) related to one or both of their soon-to-be-Path's themes, and pursuing that Mystery well past the point when any normal World of Darkness mortal would give up and go home. When they finally overcome the Lie, that initial Obsession gives way to their Path, which will continue to be defined by those themes. Paths are a much more meaningful guide to developing a character, and specifically, a <i>mage</i>, when they're not just power-sets, but also an indicator of the kind of things a PC is so consumed with investigating that they tear apart the laws of physics to find out. This will be better supported by the mechanics of 2E, but I think you can start incorporating it already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T15:23:16-08:00","id":323197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=321792#post321792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]<br /> Phobos: Thanks for the input. It sounds like from your experience starting as sleepers is the way to go. And I would like to hear peoples input on &quot;priming&quot; the sleeper characters for awakening as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to be of service!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=321800#post321800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I would now run a preAwakening game now, based on previews, I would go with other route her - first, as always, I would ask player about the Path they are aspire to. Proximi have them built in to them, but others you can always ask &quot;Choose two Arcana you want for PC, one will be more important for character&quot;. Probably they choose some Arcana that makes cool character &quot;refilling&quot; concept - like Mastigos with Spirit, becuase <b>player</b> wants to have Mind and Spirit, with first dominant. Then I would enforce in the story the life crisis on the PC the Paths are connected to - Acanthus would need to decide to forsake his all life background to search for Mystery the group is looking - or <b>she could not look for what she wants ever again. </b>Moros will need to &quot;let it go&quot; of his belongings, so he could fuel his reaserch. Obrimos will need to answer the questions on reality and his belief - in science or God - questioning. Connecting it with main plot of the game, with only a bit personal sidestep, would be best for this kind scenario. Those &quot;personality traits&quot; shown in previews are unimportant - life crisis in the play are. At the end of the game you will look on character and say &quot;Samael , when he was only John, was very possesive. But then he was Awakening as Moros he change after this and that ordeal&quot;. And a like - traits aren't really important in RPG, decisions are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Those are great ideas! Never thought to implement the path's themes as decisions for the characters to make, rather than pre-established personality traits. Thanks for the advice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=321828#post321828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would find it more interesting to just letting them play and when it comes time to Awaken and they have picked their Paths ask them (in or out-of-character) what makes Joe Z Obrimos. How did Jane A connect with the Lunargent Thorn? And so on. It helps break stereotypes and the players can come up with some really interesting ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree it's better to not constrain the players with stereotypes, but I'm the only one who has read the mage corebook, so I'll try to show them the path's using the suggested concepts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=321948#post321948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a small note:<br /> 1 - If your players are new to nWOD, the Order politics may become confusing, so either create a strong backstory to explain why they SHOULD have each other's back and not their order's, or have all players recruited by the same order, and if variety is demanded by players, try to guide them into complimentary orders for your story.<br /> <br /> 2 - Try to keep all relationshhips dynamic and recoverable (at first), a 3 party relationship helps. (e.g. the player has a mentor (little 'm', not the Background, in the same Order and when the player wants to go against one party, the other can support their desire), It also help deflect punishment to the alternate party, when needed.<br /> <br /> 3 - If you browse through David's Broken Diamond campaign, he has the players in a New Cabal, since the Concilium politics, make growing any established cabal too threatening the D.C. Council.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhostTurtle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=322371#post322371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an addendum to Gideon's suggestions, make sure the PCs have a back-story establishing that they are used to working together. It's easy for mage games to become paralyzed by over-cautious introduction scenes (&quot;Does this guy know about magic?&quot;). Either place them all in a cabal together, or if you have them start as Sleepers, make sure they all know and work together pre-Awakening.<br /> <br /> In terms of the splats getting better fleshed out, here's what I've gathered:<br /> [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the ideas! I'm thinking in making the player's characters a team as sleepers, showing them the themes of the paths and philosophies of the orders in the way to their awakening and the political stuff at the end.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3456-sir-phobos","name":"Sir Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T17:47:32-08:00","id":324904,"title":"","content":"If you do start them as a team of Sleepers, who ALL Awaken near the same time, this is Unusual, this is a &quot;clear indication of a Archmaster-level Fatebinding of Sleepers&quot;, the various factions would be either nervous, excited or opportunistic about this. <br /> <br /> This would eventually concern a group of Sleepers, that they are being controlled, or manipulated. <br /> <br /> Their Cabal forming could be the Quiessence for an Archmaster's Ascension. And if it is not, someone might just think so, and act accordingly. <br /> Its also, a great way to tie them into an Epic over-arching plotline... Unless you don't play that way. Then, at its most mundane, its just a nearly impossible coincidence, that will slowly drive at least one player mad, as they try to find the hidden meaning, that never existed...<br /> <br /> I like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T20:26:44-08:00","id":325022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Phobos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the ideas! I'm thinking in making the player's characters a team as sleepers, showing them the themes of the paths and philosophies of the orders in the way to their awakening and the political stuff at the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem! I'm not sure how you want to sequence the introduction of material, but in the Order post Dave also mentions that Sleepwalkers can now buy the first dot of Order status, as part of showing the Orders' influence behind the scenes of Sleeper organizations. Whether they buy the dot or not, maybe your players could begin to be &quot;recruited&quot; by their Orders before they Awaken (or are suspected of Awakening). A future Thearch could find herself being offered an entry-level job by a charitable non-profit she's never heard of that has really classy (but kind of occult-looking) letterhead. A future Arrow could end up having conversations about honor and integrity with his old high-school football buddy who seems not to have aged a day or gained a pound, even though he does most of his tackling in front of a jury now.<br /> <br /> When they Awaken, the would-be Thearch recognizes the letterhead as runes, providing a conduit for a spell being cast over the whole organization. She confronts her boss, and is invited to apply for a new position in the <i>real </i>organization. The Arrow detects that his friend is magically Oathbound to protect his underprivileged clients, and asks if there's any way he can help fight the good fight- his friend smiles, and says they should really start working out together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=324904#post324904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do start them as a team of Sleepers, who ALL Awaken near the same time, this is Unusual, this is a &quot;clear indication of a Archmaster-level Fatebinding of Sleepers&quot;, the various factions would be either nervous, excited or opportunistic about this.<br /> <br /> [SNIP]<br /> ... Unless you don't play that way. Then, at its most mundane, its just a nearly impossible coincidence, that will slowly drive at least one player mad, as they try to find the hidden meaning, that never existed...<br /> <br /> I like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's even more angles you could take this:<br /> <br /> If you want to build in flexibility about how you/the PCs interpret their mass Awakening, you can run that session as a series of vignettes. Instead of all of them Awakening in the course of some enormous Mystery Play that they all interpret from different angles (assuming they Awaken to different Paths), the session is just a series of short stories of all of them Awakening, one by one, over the course of a week, a month, or a year, during which it is implied the ones who hadn't Awakened yet didn't feel like they could really talk to the others about the deeply personal experience they've just had. Everyone gets their own Awakening scene, with the other characters playing supporting roles. Then, in the critical scene of the session, they all just collectively realize and admit to one another that everyone is Awakened now, and resolve to seek out Mage society.<br /> <br /> If you want to do the mass Awakening but have it be of only moderate importance, you could also just assume the Pentacle doesn't interpret it (immediately) in &quot;must be an archmaster's plan&quot; terms (partly because most mages in-setting know very little about archmages and what they can do). They'll think it's very odd and probably meaningful, and a Mystagogue might thoroughly document them (maybe even attach this Mystagogue to the party for a while as part field researcher, part NPC guide to Awakened society) but they won't know what to make of it. Some will be inclined to interpret it as a signal from the Oracles or a sign of the weakening Lie. They will likely be <i>very </i>interested in any cabal ritual symbolism the PCs decide to adopt, if they choose to form their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T02:43:40-07:00","id":1482233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/321617-how-to-intruduce-new-players-to-m-taw-right-now?p=323197#post323197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad to be of service!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Those are great ideas! Never thought to implement the path's themes as decisions for the characters to make at <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><a href=\"https://topcvwritersuk.com/citycv-review/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">topcvwritersuk.com/citycv-review/</span></a></span></span>, rather than pre-established personality traits. Thanks for the advice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree it's better to not constrain the players with stereotypes, but I'm the only one who has read the mage corebook, so I'll try to show them the path's using the suggested concepts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for the ideas! I'm thinking in making the player's characters a team as sleepers, showing them the themes of the paths and philosophies of the orders in the way to their awakening and the political stuff at the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with this. Some months ago I tried to play M:TAw after 8 years of no roleplaying, with a group of friends that had not played nWoD before, and it was also the first time I played Mage (and I was the ST), so it was kind of messy. The game stopped because of reasons, but I'm planning to start over again with the same group the next year, and I'm planning to do what Wyrdhamster is suggesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27443-fillipyang7","name":"fillipyang7","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}